  "nutshell": [
    "- China’s crude imports rose 8% y-o-y to 362.2m tonnes, re-",
    "- flecting resilient demand growth. (Page 1)",
    "- Saudi Arabia is top supplier, but its shrinking share signals",
    "- China’s diversification toward Atlantic barrels. (Page 1)",
    "- About 9% of global tankers—mostly US-linked and non-",
    "- China-built—face new Chinese port fees. (Page 1)",
    "- Potential rerouting of US-linked crude carriers could tighten",
    "- Pacific tonnage and boost freight volatility.  (Page 1)",
    "- WTI crude slid to $57.2/bbl, hitting six-month lows amid",
    "- oversupply fears . (Page 8)"
